{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"ad94725834151f6e","type":"text","text":"[[Periodic Table]]\nTable classifying different types of atoms called *elements*\n\n![[Periodic Table-1782608328024.webp]]","x":-140,"y":-125,"width":580,"height":505},
		{"id":"df67188d96454149","type":"text","text":"[[Metals]] are atoms that like to lose electrons, forming cations","x":-680,"y":-280,"width":345,"height":102},
		{"id":"3452cbb726eb8f9a","type":"text","text":"[[Alloy|Alloys]] are mixtures of metal e.g. steel","x":-1097,"y":-413,"width":250,"height":73},
		{"id":"169f395bceb76ef3","type":"text","text":"[[Metallic Bonding]] is a strong electrostatic force between cations and delocalised electrons","x":-1169,"y":-240,"width":322,"height":103},
		{"id":"9d4a5c5438352ad7","type":"text","text":"**Delocalised electrons** are free-moving electrons with no fixed position","x":-1220,"y":-80,"width":337,"height":82},
		{"id":"13d8676c6c98ea8b","type":"file","file":"01 Resources/Attachments/Metallic Bonding-1784353557700.webp","x":-1720,"y":-454,"width":400,"height":374},
		{"id":"5b2a9fa0b1c5eaa6","type":"text","text":"A [[Mole]] is a specific number of anything","x":-720,"y":320,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"7faa632dafe4252f","type":"text","text":"[[Molarity]] is measure of concentration of solution ($M$)","x":-1220,"y":242,"width":327,"height":78},
		{"id":"fd30ba109ad51473","type":"text","text":"$$C = \\frac{n}{V}$$","x":-1600,"y":146,"width":280,"height":96},
		{"id":"42b9591a9ab50705","type":"text","text":"[[Molar Mass]] is the measurement of the weight of a substance ","x":-1160,"y":380,"width":277,"height":100},
		{"id":"a5855770c22dc592","type":"text","text":"Example: [[Molar Mass]] of $NaCl$ is $50.44~g/mol$ ","x":-1540,"y":370,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"35fa7510734238d7","type":"text","text":"[[Transition Metals]] change charge (in groups 3-12)","x":-978,"y":-580,"width":250,"height":80},
		{"id":"63cc285367b07fc6","type":"text","text":"Example: Iron can be $Fe^{2+}$ or $Fe^{3+}$","x":-1360,"y":-700,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"00886ee3d95fcd57","type":"text","text":"**Chemistry**","x":680,"y":76,"width":250,"height":50},
		{"id":"e2c2954168c22f62","type":"text","text":"**Forces**","x":1120,"y":-340,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"1d2b6fecf1f9497c","type":"text","text":"**Molecules**","x":1100,"y":280,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"6c13cc8cf11101b9","type":"text","text":"**Specific**","x":1400,"y":540,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"e01cb3b289bd641a","type":"text","text":"**Groups**","x":1460,"y":128,"width":250,"height":63},
		{"id":"447618007d0bfe26","type":"text","text":"[[Aldehydes]] = Carbon bonded to $R$, a hydrogen atom and double bonded to an oxygen atom","x":1898,"y":-17,"width":341,"height":118},
