		{"id":"dd8d7f64ad9f5fe6","type":"text","text":"[[Paracetemol (Acetaminophen)]] is a polar pain killer (polar due to hydroxyl + amino group)","x":1765,"y":418,"width":335,"height":122},
		{"id":"f56e4ad77c56dd42","type":"file","file":"01 Resources/Attachments/Paracetemol (Acetaminophen)-1776577196075.webp","x":2240,"y":340,"width":260,"height":139},
		{"id":"343d0cbd598fc3fd","type":"text","text":"[[Acids]]\n- pH < 7","x":-689,"y":714,"width":364,"height":106},
		{"id":"fe36fd24f24a5856","type":"text","text":"An [[Arrhenius Acid]] is any substance that increases concentration of hydrogen ions ($H^+$) when dissolved in water.","x":-1220,"y":625,"width":326,"height":142},
		{"id":"0f866a8d67b28ab1","type":"text","text":"[[Naming Acids]]","x":-1181,"y":960,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"918e06d5c24c60f7","type":"text","text":"[[Amino Acids]] are the fundamental building blocks of [[Proteins]]","x":-1290,"y":808,"width":330,"height":84},
		{"id":"c24dec7e1d83e8b6","type":"text","text":"An [[Isomer]] is a molecule with the same empirical formula but a different structure.","x":269,"y":-540,"width":341,"height":77},
		{"id":"c3b5847368bcf860","type":"file","file":"01 Resources/Attachments/Isomer-1781917943415.webp","x":-45,"y":-862,"width":400,"height":149},
		{"id":"7ff090f23c6b5e94","type":"text","text":"cis = hydrogen atoms on same side \ntrans = hydrogens on opposite sides","x":-354,"y":-1042,"width":316,"height":103},
		{"id":"8827c83c23c33909","type":"text","text":"[[Hydrogen Bonding]] occurs between a hydrogen atom bonded to $N, O, F$ and attracted to a neighbouring molecule ","x":1743,"y":-836,"width":399,"height":123},
		{"id":"7bf6a071802f4de6","type":"text","text":"[[Polar]] = Slightly more electronegative at some parts of a molecule, due to temporary, instantaneous positions of electrons.","x":1770,"y":-1356,"width":433,"height":130},
		{"id":"67c780c52ead89af","type":"text","text":"[[Dipole-Dipole Forces]]","x":2278,"y":-716,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"675ad190ea901131","type":"text","text":"[[Non Polar]] = opposite, perfectly equal electronegativity throughout molecule","x":2403,"y":-1371,"width":461,"height":80},
		{"id":"57d2ccde06adf213","type":"text","text":"[[Dipole-Dipole Forces]] occur","x":1693,"y":-1576,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"771d617fc785c9b3","type":"file","file":"01 Resources/Attachments/London Dispersion Forces-1781306788133.webp","x":2203,"y":-1106,"width":400,"height":210},
		{"id":"75f64616aaf703d0","type":"text","text":"**Intermolecular Forces** occur *between* molecules","x":1363,"y":-896,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"13c7d0b6413c6f99","type":"text","text":"[[London Dispersion Forces]] - Weak temporary forces caused by electronegativity shifts by the temporary positions of electrons","x":1683,"y":-1076,"width":424,"height":108},
		{"id":"8e670cddc76081bf","type":"text","text":"**Intramolecular Forces** occur *inside* a molecule","x":1520,"y":-375,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"dc42361e33bac49f","type":"text","text":"[[Covalent Bonding]] are strong intramolecular forces between atoms","x":1920,"y":-280,"width":445,"height":81},
